/-!
# Surjectivity of the canonical map to the dualizing module of the blowup

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] with `A` carrying a dualizing module `ω_A` and not regular, let
`X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal, `i : E ⟶ X` its exceptional divisor and
`ω_X` the dualizing module of `X`. Clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] says that the canonical map
`f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is surjective. This file proves it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.range_exceptionalImmersion`: the exceptional divisor is the
  fibre over the closed point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap`: the surjectivity, for an
  arbitrary dualizing module `ω_X` on the blowup together with the [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] datum `D`.
  Its only input beyond those is the global generation of `ω_X|_E`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_dualizingPullbackMap_of_normalized`: the conclusion of
  **clause (3)** from the global generation `G`, for the `ω_X` the source names — the dualizing
  module normalized relative to `ω_A`. It specialises the previous theorem, and the normalization
  replaces both of the previous theorem's inputs about `ω_X`: see below. Clause (1) of the tag is
  not among its inputs.

## The argument

The source argues that `ω_X` is generated by its global sections and that its global sections are
`ω_A`. Written out, that is three steps.

*Global sections of `ω_X` restrict onto global sections of `ω_X|_E`.* The restriction sequence
`0 ⟶ ω_X(1) ⟶ ω_X ⟶ i_*(ω_X|_E) ⟶ 0`, whose second map is the canonical restriction — the unit
of `i^* ⊣ i_*`, pinned there by `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
`.exists_shortExact_schemeTwist_dualizing_unit` — and the vanishing `H¹(X, ω_X(1)) = 0` —
clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64], `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
`.isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingTwist_of_restrictionVanishing`, at `n = 1` — make
`Γ(X, ω_X) ⟶ Γ(E, ω_X|_E)` surjective through the long exact cohomology sequence. Nothing in
that step is an input of the theorem below: the sequence and the vanishing of
[Stacks, Tag 02O1] it rests on are proved in `BlowUpDualizingSequence.lean` and
`BlowUpEventualVanishing.lean`, and the curve vanishing `H¹(E, (ω_X|_E)(n)) = 0` that clause (2)
consumes is proved from the global generation `G` in
`…/RationalSingularities/ExceptionalGlobalGenerationVanishing.lean`.

*Global sections of `ω_X` lift along the canonical map.* The canonical map is the adjunct of the
*invertible* inverse trace, so it is split on global sections:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.surjective_appTop_dualizingPullbackMap`. This is
where `H⁰(X, ω_X) = ω_A` — [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] — enters.

*Generation along `E` gives generation.* A generating family of global sections of `ω_X|_E`
therefore lifts to global sections of `f^*ω_A`, so the canonical map is an epimorphism after
restriction to `E`; and an epimorphism onto a module of finite type is detected on the fibre over
the closed point, because `f` is proper and `A` is local
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.epi_of_epi_pullback_of_range_eq_fibre`). The source leaves
this last step implicit: it proves generation only along `E`.

## The inputs of clause (3)

The form of clause (3) proved here has **one** input, the global generation `G`. Clause (3)
itself, with `G` discharged, is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_normalizedPullbackMap` of
`…/RationalSingularities/BlowUpNormalizedDualizingGeneration.lean`. The restriction
sequence is not among them, neither is the [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] datum `D`, neither is clause (1) of
the tag itself, and neither — this is new — is the curve vanishing of [Stacks, Tag 0B62].

* **The curve vanishing is not an input: `G` proves it.** What clause (2) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B64] consumes, as `BlowUpDualizingSequence.lean` states it, is
  `H¹(E, (ω_X|_E)(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ 0` — phrased at the restriction `ω_X|_E` itself, so that
  clause (1) of the tag, the isomorphism `ω_E ≅ (ω_X|_E)(-1)`, and the [Stacks, Tag 0B62]
  vanishing `H¹(E, ω_E(n+1)) = 0` are two possible routes to it rather than inputs. Neither is
  taken here. A module on `E` generated by its global sections has vanishing first cohomology in
  every twist `n ≥ 0`, by clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0B63] and the commutation of `H¹(E, -)`
  with direct sums, and `ω_X|_E` is such a module by `G`; that is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_of_generatingSections` of
  `…/RationalSingularities/ExceptionalGlobalGenerationVanishing.lean`. The `ω_X`-twisted
  restriction sequence — whose monomorphy says that the local equation of `E` is a
  nonzerodivisor on `ω_X` — the eventual vanishing of [Stacks, Tag 02O1] and the descent from
  large `n` are proved in `BlowUpDualizingSequence.lean` and `BlowUpEventualVanishing.lean`, and
  so are absent from the statement below too.
* `G` is the global generation of `ω_X|_E = ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)`, which is [Stacks, Tag 0B5H]. That tag
  is formalized in this development as `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_tensorSheaf`, whose *statement* places no hypothesis on the base
  field but which carries five hypotheses of its own on the curve; applying it to `E` therefore
  does not discharge `G`, and the conclusion is an input here. The application itself *is*
  performed, in `ExceptionalDualizingGeneration.lean`: `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_dualityInputs` produces `G` from exactly those
  five hypotheses at `E` — `hdual`, clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2]; `hone`,
  `dim_κ H¹(E, ω_E) = 1` of Section [Stacks, Tag 0B5B]; `hnosub`, the absence of a submodule of
  `ω_X|_E` supported in dimension zero; `hd`, the degree bound `deg 𝒪_E(1) ≥ 2` of clause (3)
  of [Stacks, Tag 0B63]; and `hsec`, the vanishing section of [Stacks, Tag 0B58] with its
  global-section count — and discharges everything else, including Situation
  [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] at `E`, the identification of `ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)` with `ω_X|_E` and all the
  coherence side conditions. Of the five, `hd` is proved:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.two_le_invertibleCurveDegree_curveTwistSheaf_one` of
  `ExceptionalTwistDegree.lean` proves it from `¬ IsRegularLocalRing S.A` alone.
* **The residue field is where `G` stops, and not through a hypothesis on it.** Neither
  [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] at the shape above nor its application to `E` assumes `κ` algebraically
  closed; what is true is that `hsec` is *unsatisfiable* over a `κ` that is not — the
  counterexample, a closed point of degree three on `ℙ¹_ℚ`, is in the module documentation of
  `Curves/VanishingResults/DualizingTwistGeneration.lean`. So `G` cannot be reached by
  discharging `hsec` at this spelling, and the only route left is the source's own: prove
  [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] over `κ̄`, where it is formalized as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_dualizing_tensorSheaf_of_isAlgClosed`, and descend by base
  change. The descent needs part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0E32] for `ω_E`, which is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.pullbackDualizingSheafOverFieldIso` of
  `Curves/VanishingResults/DualizingSheafBaseChangeIso.lean`, proved from duality rather than from
  the twisted inverse image. Through the twisted inverse image it would be blocked: the
  [Stacks, Tag 0A9K] it rests on *is* registered, but only for a
  base change along an open immersion — `Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion`
  `.isIso_twistedInverseImagePushforwardBaseChange_of_isOpenImmersion` of
  `…/Duality/OpenImmersion/TwistedInverseImageRestrictionBaseChange.lean`, and
  `Stacks.Duality.isIso_refinementXi` for a compactification square — and `E_{κ̄} ⟶ E` is a
  field extension, so the Tor-independent generality the descent needs is the part that is
  genuinely absent, as that file's own attribute string records.

  A second potential blocker does not arise. The algebraically
  closed statement is taken at the canonical `Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField` of
  `E ⟶ Spec(κ)`, whereas clause (1) of this tag delivers `ω_E = H¹(a(ω_X))`, which is only *a*
  dualizing module ([Stacks, Tag 0A7F]) — and the two are identified, as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
  `.nonempty_exceptionalDualizingModule_iso_dualizingSheafOverField` of
  `…/Duality/ExceptionalDualizingSheafIdentification.lean`, which closes clause (2) of this tag
  and goes through [Stacks, Tag 0A9F] rather than [Stacks, Tag 0AA2], the cohomological reading
  of [Stacks, Tag 0A7M], and [Stacks, Tag 0A9X] at the locally small model.
* **`G` is equivalent to the conclusion.** The source `f^*ω_A` of the canonical map is generated
  by its global sections for a formal reason — all elements of `ω_A` span it, and pullback
  carries global generating sections to global generating sections — so an epimorphism onto
  `ω_X` restricts along `i` to an epimorphism onto `ω_X|_E`, making `ω_X|_E` globally generated.
  That converse is `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
  `.nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_of_epi` of
  `…/RationalSingularities/BlowUpDualizingGenerationEquivalence.lean`, and with
  `epi_dualizingPullbackMap` it gives the equivalence
  `nonempty_generatingSections_restriction_iff_epi`. So `G` is not an auxiliary input that a
  cheaper statement on `E` might discharge: it is this clause, read on `E`. The same holds of
  the stronger normalization `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
  `.DualizingNormalization`, under which `G` becomes *true* — it is then the source's own lemma
  — without becoming *proved*.
* `D` is the datum of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] that
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.bijective_trace` takes, namely
  Grauert–Riemenschneider vanishing [Stacks, Tag 0AXD] and the duality exact sequence
  [Stacks, Tag 0B4S]. Without it the canonical map does not exist. **It is not an input of
  clause (3).** `epi_dualizingPullbackMap_of_normalized` takes instead the normalization of
  `ω_X` relative to `ω_A` — `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
  `.NormalizedDualizingModule`, the condition [Stacks, Remark 0B4R] imposes on *the* dualizing
  module of `X` — and `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation`
  `.dualizingTraceSequenceOfNormalized` produces `D` from it, the trace of a normalized
  dualizing module being invertible by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.bijective_trace_of_normalized`. The
  normalization also supplies the dualizing hypothesis `hωX`, so clause (3) has two inputs,
  not five.

**What the normalization does not do is remove `G`, and no proof can.** `N` is relative duality
in degree zero, and it does not separate `ω_X` from `ω_X(E)`: an `A` for which both are
normalized while `ω_X(E)|_E` is not generated by its global sections (and `H¹(X, ω_X(E)) ≠ 0`),
with the verification, is in the implementation notes of
`…/RationalSingularities/NormalizedDualizingModule.lean`. So `G` is independent of `N`. It is
also *necessary*, which is the stronger statement: for that same
`A = ℚ[x, y, z]/(xz − y²)` localized at `(x, y, z)`, with `ω_A = A` and the normalized
`ω_X = 𝒪_X(E)`, the trace is the identity on `Γ(X, 𝒪_X(E)) = A`, so the canonical map
`f^*ω_A = 𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_X(E)` of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is the inclusion, whose cokernel is
`i_*(𝒪_X(E)|_E) = i_*𝒪_{ℙ¹}(-2) ≠ 0`. The conclusion of clause (3) therefore *fails* for a
module satisfying `N`, so `G` cannot be deleted from the statement below at all; only
strengthening `N` to the source's own
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.DualizingNormalization`, which pins `ω_X` down
up to isomorphism by `…DualizingNormalization.moduleIso`, would make `G` true — and proving it
there is still [Stacks, Tag 0B5H], with both of the blockers listed above.

**Non-regularity of `A` is the source's own restriction on `A` and is not used by the proof.**
The statement would be false-by-vacuity without it rather than more general: it is what
`hcurve` and `G` need. For `A` regular, `E ≅ 𝐏¹_κ` and `ω_X|_E ≅ 𝒪_E(-1)`, which is not
generated by its global sections, so `G` cannot be supplied; `A` not regular is what makes
`deg 𝒪_E(1) ≥ 2`, which is how non-regularity enters [Stacks, Tag 0B63] and thence those two
inputs. It is therefore recorded, unused.

